WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:07.412
You'll write the weekly digest, and read
its five sections as an owner would.

3
00:00:07.412 --> 00:00:12.163
You'll record a collection, a
routing run and a digest as evidence,

4
00:00:12.163 --> 00:00:16.287
and say which steps, controls
and K S I's each record names.

5
00:00:16.287 --> 00:00:19.254
You'll check the evidence
chain and the checksum file,

6
00:00:19.254 --> 00:00:21.950
and show that an edit
after recording fails both.

7
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.705
You'll check a stage's coverage,

8
00:00:23.705 --> 00:00:27.075
and name the steps a test stage
and a production stage need.

9
00:00:27.075 --> 00:00:30.696
And you'll read the runbook's
promotion go/no-go criteria,

10
00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:33.687
and say which ones the
evidence check answers.

11
00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:39.338
You need Module 7 first, because this lab
repeats its two collections and routings.

12
00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:44.637
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1 or
later with Pester 5, and no tenant.

13
00:00:44.637 --> 00:00:50.350
Lab 2 uses a run folder from an earlier
module's Lab 2, kept on agency storage.
